  "body": "Right now, [`HIDDevice.forget()` step 2](https://hid.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-dom-hiddevice-forget-2) starts with:\n\n> Perform the following steps [in parallel](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#in-parallel):\n>  1. For each device of this.\\[\\[devices\\]\\]:\n        1. If device does not share device access permissions with the HIDDevice, then continue to the next device.\n        2. Set device.\\[\\[state\\]\\] to \"forgetting\".\n\n`this.[[devices]]` seems to refer to [`HID.devices`](https://hid.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-devices), but `this` should be a `HIDDevice` in this context. I think this is just a mistake and `HIDDevice.forget()` should just act on the `this` device.",
